        -:  151:/**
        -:  152: * @brief      Dynamic bitset.
        -:  153: *
        -:  154: * @details    Data structure used to store a vector of bits and apply binary operations to it. The
        -:  155: *             bits are stored in an optimized way in an underling block type. It is highly inspired
        -:  156: *             by std\::bitset but with a run-time changeable size.
        -:  157: *
        -:  158: *             Preconditions are checked with @a assert but no exception will be thrown if one is
        -:  159: *             violated (as with std\::bitset).
        -:  160: *
        -:  161: * @remark     It is not a Container as it does not provide iterators because of the reference proxy
        -:  162: *             class used to access the bits.
        -:  163: *
        -:  164: * @tparam     Block      Block type to use for storing the bits, must be an unsigned integral type
        -:  165: * @tparam     Allocator  Allocator type to use for memory management, must meet the standard
        -:  166: *                        requirements of @a Allocator
        -:  167: *
        -:  168: * @since      1.0.0
        -:  169: */
        -:  170:template<typename Block = unsigned long long, typename Allocator = std::allocator<Block>>
