        -: 1589:	 * @details    The size comparison is necessary for the comparison operators to keep their
        -: 1590:	 *             properties. For example without the size comparison the "<=" operator (defined
        -: 1591:	 *             for "A <= B" by "!(B < A)") would no longer be antisymmetric (if A \<= B and B
        -: 1592:	 *             \<= A, then A == B) because @ref operator==() compare the @ref
        -: 1593:	 *             sul::dynamic_bitset as a container and not a number. For example with bitsets
        -: 1594:	 *             A(0011) and B(011), without the size comparison B \< A would be @a false, A \<= B
        -: 1595:	 *             would be @a true, B \<= A would be @a true, but A == B would be @a false,
        -: 1596:	 *             breaking the antisymmetric property of the operator. Thus, to respect the
        -: 1597:	 *             properties of the operators, the size is used as a secondary criteria for the
        -: 1598:	 *             comparison of @ref sul::dynamic_bitset which content represent the same number.
